From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - ChFi3d: fillets whose arcs cross are no longer taken for a touching pair

Two fillets on the opposite edges of a face whose radii add up to more than its width
(a 4 x 10 x 6 box, 3 and 3) were reported done with a solid that BRepCheck rejects and whose
volume is above the box's (315 for 240). The 8.0.1 builder refused them. Part 2 of the fillet
handling (#1449) accepts tangential contacts and rejects transversal ones, but a crossing of
the end-cap arcs is reported by Geom2dInt_GInter as a segment about the tolerance long, with
no point, and ChFi3d_HasTransversalIntersection looked at points only.

A segment is now a crossing when the two curves are not tangent at it, unless it joins the
ends of both curves. The fillets are refused again, as in 8.0.1.

DRAW case blend complex H4 carried a TODO for the faulty shape its fillet returned; it now expects the refusal and keeps the old check for the day the fillet is built.

Related to #1568 and #1177. The GTest checks that no such solid is reported done.

Upstream: Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT#1667 (fork branch SecondMouseAU/OCCT fix/chfi3d-crossing-arcs). This is the form of that
pull request as it stacks on the earlier patches of this series; where it differs from the pull request
as submitted it is only in the lines the stack made conflict (see Scripts/patches/README.md). The DRAW
test cases under tests/ that the pull request edits are not part of this patch: the build has no Draw.

---
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.cxx
index 37491f8104..75f68ffedd 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.cxx
@@ -3346,7 +3346,16 @@ void ChFi3d_FilDS(const int                         SolidIndex,
 
 //=======================================================================
 
-bool ChFi3d_HasTransversalIntersection(const Geom2dInt_GInter& theIntersector)
+namespace
+{
+//! Sine of the largest angle between two curves that still counts as tangent.
+constexpr double THE_TANGENT_SIN = 1.e-6;
+} // namespace
+
+bool ChFi3d_HasTransversalIntersection(const Geom2dInt_GInter&    theIntersector,
+                                       const Geom2dAdaptor_Curve& theFirstCurve,
+                                       const Geom2dAdaptor_Curve& theSecondCurve,
+                                       const double               theTolerance)
 {
   for (int anIndex = 1; anIndex <= theIntersector.NbPoints(); ++anIndex)
   {
@@ -3359,6 +3368,36 @@ bool ChFi3d_HasTransversalIntersection(const Geom2dInt_GInter& theIntersector)
       return true;
     }
   }
+  // Curves that cross are reported as a segment, not a point: a crossing unless tangent there.
+  for (int anIndex = 1; anIndex <= theIntersector.NbSegments(); ++anIndex)
+  {
+    const IntRes2d_IntersectionSegment& aSegment = theIntersector.Segment(anIndex);
+    if (!aSegment.HasFirstPoint() || !aSegment.HasLastPoint())
+    {
+      continue;
+    }
+    const IntRes2d_IntersectionPoint& aFirstPoint = aSegment.FirstPoint();
+    const auto                        isEnd = [theTolerance](const double               theParameter,
+                                      const Geom2dAdaptor_Curve& theCurve) {
+      return std::abs(theParameter - theCurve.FirstParameter()) <= theTolerance
+             || std::abs(theParameter - theCurve.LastParameter()) <= theTolerance;
+    };
+    if (isEnd(aFirstPoint.ParamOnFirst(), theFirstCurve)
+        && isEnd(aFirstPoint.ParamOnSecond(), theSecondCurve))
+    {
+      continue; // the curves join end to end: not a crossing
+    }
+    gp_Pnt2d aPoint;
+    gp_Vec2d aFirstTangent, aSecondTangent;
+    theFirstCurve.D1(aFirstPoint.ParamOnFirst(), aPoint, aFirstTangent);
+    theSecondCurve.D1(aFirstPoint.ParamOnSecond(), aPoint, aSecondTangent);
+    const double aNorms = aFirstTangent.Magnitude() * aSecondTangent.Magnitude();
+    if (aNorms > gp::Resolution()
+        && std::abs(aFirstTangent.Crossed(aSecondTangent)) > THE_TANGENT_SIN * aNorms)
+    {
+      return true;
+    }
+  }
   return false;
 }
 
@@ -3549,7 +3588,7 @@ void ChFi3d_StripeEdgeInter(const occ::handle<ChFiDS_Stripe>& theStripe1,
       {
         DStr.MergeEquivalentCurves(aFI1.LineIndex(), aFI2.LineIndex(), isReversed);
       }
-      if (ChFi3d_HasTransversalIntersection(anIntersector))
+      if (ChFi3d_HasTransversalIntersection(anIntersector, aPCurve1, aPCurve2, tol2d))
       {
         throw StdFail_NotDone("StripeEdgeInter : fillets have too big radiuses");
       }
